FairDerm-Eval

FairDerm-Eval audits melanoma diagnostic fairness, explanation quality, calibration, cross-modality behavior, and clinician plus model deployment outcomes across public dermatology datasets and a restricted deployment cohort.

Installation

pip install -e .
conda env create -f environment.yml
python -m fairderm_eval.cli.audit settings/main/audit.yaml

Docker

docker build -f containers/CUDA121.lock .

Data

Dataset source links are listed in records/dataset_sources.txt. Private deployment records are not public and are represented only by aggregate tables.

Training

The primary supervised baseline configuration uses 8 GPUs, global batch 1536, 200 epochs, learning rate 0.00003, bf16 mixed precision, and 518x518 images. This mirrors the reported audit scale where training details were incomplete and uses an upper-bound compute profile for local baseline runs.

Evaluation

python -m fairderm_eval.cli.audit settings/main/audit.yaml
python -m fairderm_eval.cli.tables records/tables/ddi_reference.json
python -m fairderm_eval.cli.train settings/testonly/two_step.yaml

Expected headline values

DDI GPT-5: FNR disparity 18.2 percentage points, AUC gap 5.6 percentage points, worst-group ratio 0.79.
Human plus AI deployment: FNR disparity 7.4 percentage points and worst-group ratio 0.92.

Compute budget

Primary audit settings reserve 8 accelerator processes, 80 GB memory per process, bf16 precision, and a 96 hour wall-clock envelope for full public dataset evaluation with prompt collection, explanation scoring, and supervised baselines.

Checkpoints

Model checkpoints are available upon reasonable request. Hashes for public release artifacts should be recorded in artifacts when frozen.
